#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489274 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119857 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f644bed-7adb-5907-87b4-99b1902e7850" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Basis of the Space Spanned by a Set of Vectors by Identifying Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28f8bb97-2bc4-5dc8-af62-80dc0012c72c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488556} {:answer/id #uuid "769b2e11-b333-500c-84a5-51aa4d8c16b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488705} {:answer/id #uuid "991e9362-9655-5cf0-a0be-aaa13d573c9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488777} {:answer/id #uuid "d19e6191-26d5-53a3-95c7-65dc2640adef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488899} {:answer/id #uuid "d81d6455-dfab-5856-82d0-2c4f85caa5c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d81d6455-dfab-5856-82d0-2c4f85caa5c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488917} :answer-field/id #uuid "de1a4479-26db-5da3-9251-44ec64871f06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d77196fa-8d44-5cad-922e-bddbeed8f53e" :question/math-academy-id "q-110851" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ ${a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 & 15 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, our matrix is already in a row echelon form.\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $2$nd columns are pivot columns, while the $3$rd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nThe $1$st and $2$nd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247171 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119857 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f644bed-7adb-5907-87b4-99b1902e7850" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Basis of the Space Spanned by a Set of Vectors by Identifying Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "316d5931-7999-53f3-ad90-06c5ea96ca28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488576} {:answer/id #uuid "3cc5baa7-58c6-5fb1-bb5b-bc5d2809c3fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488596} {:answer/id #uuid "81e78e16-327e-5283-9ae6-8297686d3018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488728} {:answer/id #uuid "8961892e-bd58-5202-80e6-b3295e996c34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488743} {:answer/id #uuid "8f4f12a7-86f7-5632-aa12-4ebf32e0df03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f4f12a7-86f7-5632-aa12-4ebf32e0df03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488756} :answer-field/id #uuid "7af92bdb-0264-5972-9c25-894d9f25aaee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c69f867a-804d-5cf3-bc38-00ede80f0b28" :question/math-academy-id "q-110853" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, our matrix is already in a row echelon form.\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{3}\\},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119857 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f644bed-7adb-5907-87b4-99b1902e7850" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Basis of the Space Spanned by a Set of Vectors by Identifying Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5646c621-9ff4-5c1e-8500-97102b3d30e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427545} {:answer/id #uuid "830afe53-3ec3-5e7b-9c3c-099ac06955ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427546} {:answer/id #uuid "9ac2a6dd-782d-5d5d-9fa2-a488442ba8e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427547} {:answer/id #uuid "deb5edd7-a250-52b2-967e-5c46f246d2b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427553} {:answer/id #uuid "f5e5049e-edad-5162-bbb3-262144109a0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "deb5edd7-a250-52b2-967e-5c46f246d2b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427553} :answer-field/id #uuid "52b0b14b-3418-5c43-b479-6c5ffa179aac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427556}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd91b565-0528-53ef-9896-e748c3fd0d1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-75068" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ ${a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 16 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 16 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $2$nd columns are pivot columns, while the $3$rd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one.\n\nThe $1$st and $2$nd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489257 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119858 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b72ed196-a73b-59ab-a7c3-5173249cf7e5" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Given Set Is a Basis of a Span"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "422e2ec5-20ff-549c-9dc2-cfe71b65c008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488606} {:answer/id #uuid "806a2215-b8ec-5aa9-aeab-b5dd3e906ac7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488727} {:answer/id #uuid "86784b09-cfa3-589f-b8d3-d3ab6f43882a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488733} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b14b1e-a851-5ba2-94dc-2cad1dd6e6f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488843} {:answer/id #uuid "ef0bf52d-906e-5f34-9ed4-b19de3addea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "422e2ec5-20ff-549c-9dc2-cfe71b65c008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488606} :answer-field/id #uuid "46d3f8dc-aba1-58f4-a862-47da2d463904" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a78df4d7-9e4a-5ba6-b17f-e12077b05fb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-76325" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are given below. Determine whether $B=\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${a}_{3}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the RREF matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=4,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+4\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=1\\cdot 4=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119858 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b72ed196-a73b-59ab-a7c3-5173249cf7e5" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Given Set Is a Basis of a Span"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03b6f1cc-ac52-5722-9030-b2f70afc1e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371073} {:answer/id #uuid "505e1e00-4bbe-58cd-93f5-9ae6fca91fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371074} {:answer/id #uuid "fa7543da-eac6-5f26-be7d-c12dd0282c43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371075} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d79a33-33fd-5d1e-9b3e-6df988afd31c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371076} {:answer/id #uuid "684b58dc-c7bc-5e7a-ad38-d7e82bd7f00b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}\\}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "505e1e00-4bbe-58cd-93f5-9ae6fca91fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371074} :answer-field/id #uuid "94fadecf-d53d-561e-b319-c2fb1000fc28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "82af09e9-f65e-5eb5-8267-28d6aa4538d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-76338" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ ${a}_{3},$ and ${a}_{4}$ are given below. Determine whether $B=\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}\\}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3},$ where ${a}_{4}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{4}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}\\}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+{x}_{3}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ -9{x}_{1}-8{x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -8 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -8 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+9{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 17\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the reduced matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}\\}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=-15,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=17,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n(-15)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+0\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+17\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=(-15)+0+17=2.$"}]}
